{"title":"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A particle is located on the coordinate plane at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38ec6a35045b7cc0f04c4989a99570bcc29aee43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Define a <i>move</i> for the particle as a counterclockwise rotation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/2023fd6335b423b0090fdb6999a68778fcaa3ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> radians about the origin followed by a translation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units in the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-direction. Given that the particle's position after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e10e5f3aa7c766cb27c3ad319fa526f71588cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> moves is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b7a40ab0d8178e83fe1b91c511d04b1246059b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, find the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab457e4a9151f2c3ce6e638657ea853895380fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|p| + |q|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d0c6b840a12d05c098bfea7ef89c07993e469b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> be the position of the particle on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-plane, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the origin, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the inclination of OP to the x-axis. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9674495d4952d1601f366881ce6d56f1ef5203b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x&#39;, y&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is the position of the particle after a move from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then we have two equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a606841183a001b6a780a104a40bd9d8d8b4aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;$\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19ac5343ae3e72d247f8e2d0ec7757ae5cca2634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"17\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c24a2059e5791dbecf0282ea3bed7e46436de9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&#39;=r\\cos(\\pi/4+\\theta)+10 = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}(x - y)}{2} + 10\\]\" width=\"338\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79ce60e79deda9238e5e315c47f11f347ef2122e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y&#39; = r\\sin(\\pi/4+\\theta) = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}(x + y)}{2}.\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"41\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a56b1526cf38268aae07b6cf67ea94c8d9a55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n, y_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> be the position of the particle after the nth move, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/91492b2fddeae4f9ffb7cd370c13308852f8dc8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b225b2301dacb993e80b4b7c27158d05fe05eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b9ee6082e769961ee7076bc7bde5060dec8e400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} + y_{n+1} =  \\sqrt{2}x_n+10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b6be6f7ff4aecec01ef71a77ba5ea71ad3926b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} - y_{n+1} = -\\sqrt{2}y_n+10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"21\" />. This implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3fbcebd2059097416d900bbdfe69be5f15bd62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+2} = -y_n + 5\\sqrt{2}+ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff136567981faeae01b2fc9543b62b174caa3f58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{n+2}=x_n + 5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" />.\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/91492b2fddeae4f9ffb7cd370c13308852f8dc8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b225b2301dacb993e80b4b7c27158d05fe05eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/6/936548d59c303203eaf1480c5a1fdd557aad359c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_8 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f367103b003f18cebde9db0dc5dcfa8a0500fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_8 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> again for the first time. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd3bd55a6f7d50703fd94850b4c68a1d8595065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = x_{150} = x_6 = -5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e6caf8b9b8e0dc16377066cde3783a789654fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = y_{150} = y_6 = 5 + 5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />. Hence, the final answer is\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e93554c7f003c0766d1509e99aad3fbd7d9f19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt {2} + 5(\\sqrt {2} + 1) \\approx 19.1 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"269\" height=\"23\" /></center>\n<p>If you're curious, the points do eventually form an octagon and repeat. Seems counterintuitive, but believe it or not, it happens.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.desmos.com/calculator/febtiheosz\">https://www.desmos.com/calculator/febtiheosz</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the particle's position be represented by a complex number. Recall that multiplying a number by cis<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30ecccacb97c85f75dffede4b3c0958be5612c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\theta \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> rotates the object in the complex plane by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> counterclockwise. In this case, we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4416f188b4c2b20452eb8860454421fc58abe92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = cis(\\frac{\\pi}{4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"33\" />. Therefore, applying the rotation and shifting the coordinates by 10 in the positive x direction in the complex plane results to\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdba935af30d8eca5158fe6587d0c83bf1952d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{150} = (((5a + 10)a + 10)a + 10 \\ldots) = 5a^{150} + 10 a^{149} + 10a^{148}+ \\ldots + 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"568\" height=\"19\" /></center>\n<p>where a is cis<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30ecccacb97c85f75dffede4b3c0958be5612c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\theta \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. By De-Moivre's theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a4e8d096494550d983a3e7cbb786441a6bcad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(cis( \\theta \\right)^n )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"19\" />=cis<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/7308a5b483fb3856aad89905f25c63454fff0d10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(n \\theta \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />.\nTherefore,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe0bcb6dc41f4d96f940d2d64b59865ef9566df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10(a^{150} + \\ldots + 1)= 10(1 + a + \\ldots + a^6) = - 10(a^7) = - 10(\\frac{ \\sqrt {2} }{2} - \\frac{i\\sqrt {2}} {2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"563\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbae50fe0b2c07d70431ce7b5142e38e06ea2e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5a^{150} = - 5i$\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the final answer is\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e93554c7f003c0766d1509e99aad3fbd7d9f19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt {2} + 5(\\sqrt {2} + 1) \\approx 19.1 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"269\" height=\"23\" /></center>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>As before, consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> as a complex number.  Consider the transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7aebba29b7f3d51e5188fc13d5a99f44b3e5be36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\to (z-\\omega)e^{i\\theta} + \\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"22\" />.  This is a clockwise rotation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> radians about the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> denote one move of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  Then\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2008AIMEII9Sol3.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/61/2008AIMEII9Sol3.png/300px-2008AIMEII9Sol3.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"226\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/61/2008AIMEII9Sol3.png/450px-2008AIMEII9Sol3.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/61/2008AIMEII9Sol3.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> rotates along a circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658a190535b3e760006d0f546cd52765a392dde2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega = 5+(5+5\\sqrt2)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"24\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/88337513a24e4d74b8c38ed3b3b643836f0af4ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf1fabc934658da4210a0155b73f6027aec2c809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^9(z) = f(z) \\implies f^{150}(z) = f^6(z) \\implies p+q = \\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"425\" height=\"25\" />, as desired (the final algebra bash isn't bad).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e68bebeb4477eb2644f4820f89599f26594ee1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T:\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}\\rightarrow R(\\frac{\\pi}{4})\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"244\" height=\"45\" />. We assume that the rotation matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0284940f5a8b17197f3bc82b64519d23e12cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(\\frac{\\pi}{4}) = R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"34\" /> here. Then we have \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c779a76d8286dbe05981c0790cb34629e9605e30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T^{150}\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}=R(R(...R(R\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix})+\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}...)+\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix})+\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"534\" height=\"45\" /></center> \n<p>This simplifies to\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f6b8137274ebe4c9479bdef91f1dad1f7d7633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^{150}\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}+(I+R^2+R^3+...+R^{149})\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"349\" height=\"45\" /></center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba12e5961832c915035ed7eb5cc36c80a9ec48c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R+R^{7}=O, R^2+R^6=O, R^3+R^5=O, I+R^4=O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"20\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974084021b7ccbc19f79085c289db7eadeea3ffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^6\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}+(-R^6-R^7)\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"224\" height=\"45\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5506b4ff6cd794b1c64399712c40f1b3637948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=-5\\sqrt{2}, q=5\\sqrt{2}+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"23\" />. The answer is yet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/58939991c6b4c107fdd8c737c1473adb9a10ea0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor10\\sqrt{2}+5\\rfloor=\\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II\" title=\"2008 AIME II\">2008 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a h